# The Stilo library

Functions for Stilo documents, written in Swan. `stilo init` copies this
folder into a package's `lib/stilo/`. This document binds one name, `stilo`,
a namespace of the library's functions. A document of the package imports
`~/lib/stilo/index.texl` and binds `lib.data.stilo` as `stilo`; the Stilo
editor inserts that import when it is needed (the full tag is in Stilo's
`docs/packages.md`: it cannot be quoted here, where it would run).

Each function lives in its own document of this folder, which describes it:

- `stilo.dataframe` — a table of data (`dataframe.texl`).
- `stilo.charts` — charts drawn as SVG: `stilo.charts.line`
  (`charts.texl`).

<% texl.import "dataframe.texl" ~> (d -> (texl.import "charts.texl" ~> (c -> bind "stilo" {
    dataframe: d.data.dataframe,
    charts: c.data.charts
}))) %>
